A||||6||la9||High Idle - Red Hot Manifold||||1||
Z||000000||la9||02-20-2000||06:10 PM||||I just got my engine rebuild back together and installed. Had an oil leak but fixed that. Now the lowest it will idle is 1500rpm and after it runs awhile the firewall side manifold gets red hot. What do I need to check ? Is it a timing problem since I haven't timed it yet ? I know I've seen this problem before on here so someone give me some ideas ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||02-20-2000||07:37 PM||||Sounds like a *big* vacuum leak. Checked the EGR tube, between the EGR valve and the plenum?||||reg||1
Z||000002||cobra427||02-20-2000||07:42 PM||||Had the same exact problem. checked the EGR tube and sure enough, it was cracked where it connected to the plenum. Probable cause. I bought the braided one from IRM. If you can afford the $90.00+ ,go for it . Looks like it will last a lifetime.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||02-20-2000||07:44 PM||||If it is the v-6, make sure all of the plenum bolts are torqued to spec. That will allow for a higher idle.||||reg||1
Z||000004||la9||02-20-2000||07:59 PM||||I checked the egr tube and think it is ok. I sprayed it with wd-40 and no change in idle. didn't do the plenum side. I torqued the plenum to specs. I will probably pull the egr tube off the plenum side and plug it and see if that solves my problem. Does anyone know if I knocked one of the little lines off underneath the plenum if that would affect it enough to keep minimal idle at 1500 rpm ? I just set the timing. Keep the ideas coming I appreciate it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||02-20-2000||10:19 PM||||The only line that would allow for such a fast idle is the steel line running under the plenum. I believe one end plugs in under the plenum, and the other end plugs into the bottom of the throttle body.||||reg||1
Z||000006||la9||02-21-2000||01:23 PM||||Thanks everyone. That is what the problem was. The steel tube running from the intake into the throttle body. Now it Purrs like a kitten.||||reg||1
